# Attitudes of Community College Faculty and Students Toward the Use of Videodisc Technology in the Classroom.

**Authors:** Olson, Margot A., And Others

## Abstract
Describes a study of 15 faculty and 81 students regarding their attitudes toward the use of interactive videodisc technology, highlighting faculty perceptions of the technology, level of student interest in instructional strategies, and reaction to humanities applications. Indicates that faculty responded well to the technology and students highly recommended it. (MAB)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ515204

